🧠 LFU Cache (Design + Data Structures – Very Advanced)

This is asked in product companies like Amazon, Microsoft, Google.

It tests:

HashMap

Doubly Linked List

Frequency tracking

O(1) design thinking

🧩 Problem Statement

Design a data structure that follows Least Frequently Used (LFU) policy.

Implement:

LFUCache(int capacity)
int get(int key)
void put(int key, int value)


Rules:

1️⃣ When capacity is full, remove the least frequently used key
2️⃣ If multiple keys have same frequency → remove Least Recently Used (LRU)
3️⃣ Both get() and put() must run in O(1) time

🧪 Example
Input:
capacity = 2

put(1,1)
put(2,2)
get(1) → returns 1
put(3,3) → removes key 2
get(2) → returns -1
get(3) → returns 3

🎯 What Is This Problem Really Testing?

It is a combination of:

LRU Cache

Frequency counting

Efficient O(1) removal

This is NOT simple.

🧠 Why Normal HashMap Is Not Enough?

Because we must:

✔ Track frequency
✔ Track insertion order inside same frequency
✔ Remove least frequently used instantly

We need 3 structures.

🏗 Data Structures Used

We maintain:

1️⃣ Key → Node Map
Map<Integer, Node>

2️⃣ Frequency → Doubly Linked List
Map<Integer, DoublyLinkedList>


Each frequency has its own list.

3️⃣ Variable minFreq

Tracks minimum frequency.

📦 Node Structure

Each node stores:

key
value
frequency
prev
next

🪜 Step-by-Step Logic
🔹 GET(key)

IF key not present
→ return -1

ELSE:

Get node

Increase frequency

Move node to new frequency list

Update minFreq if needed

Return value

🔹 PUT(key, value)

If capacity = 0 → return

If key exists:

Update value

Call GET(key) logic to increase frequency

Else:
If cache full:

Remove head of minFreq list

Create new node:

freq = 1

Insert into freq 1 list

Set minFreq = 1

🔎 Dry Run Example

capacity = 2

put(1,1)
put(2,2)

State:
freq 1 → [1,2]

get(1)

freq 1 → [2]
freq 2 → [1]

put(3,3)

Remove from freq 1 → remove 2

Insert 3:
freq 1 → [3]
freq 2 → [1]

Correct behavior.

💻 Full Java Code (O(1))
import java.util.*;

class LFUCache {

    class Node {
        int key, value, freq;
        Node prev, next;

        Node(int key, int value) {
            this.key = key;
            this.value = value;
            this.freq = 1;
        }
    }

    class DoublyLinkedList {
        Node head, tail;
        int size;

        DoublyLinkedList() {
            head = new Node(0, 0);
            tail = new Node(0, 0);
            head.next = tail;
            tail.prev = head;
        }

        void add(Node node) {
            node.next = head.next;
            node.prev = head;
            head.next.prev = node;
            head.next = node;
            size++;
        }

        void remove(Node node) {
            node.prev.next = node.next;
            node.next.prev = node.prev;
            size--;
        }

        Node removeLast() {
            if (size > 0) {
                Node last = tail.prev;
                remove(last);
                return last;
            }
            return null;
        }
    }

    int capacity, minFreq;
    Map<Integer, Node> keyMap;
    Map<Integer, DoublyLinkedList> freqMap;

    public LFUCache(int capacity) {
        this.capacity = capacity;
        keyMap = new HashMap<>();
        freqMap = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public int get(int key) {

        if (!keyMap.containsKey(key)) {
            return -1;
        }

        Node node = keyMap.get(key);
        update(node);
        return node.value;
    }

    public void put(int key, int value) {

        if (capacity == 0) return;

        if (keyMap.containsKey(key)) {

            Node node = keyMap.get(key);
            node.value = value;
            update(node);

        } else {

            if (keyMap.size() == capacity) {

                DoublyLinkedList minList = freqMap.get(minFreq);
                Node removed = minList.removeLast();
                keyMap.remove(removed.key);
            }

            Node newNode = new Node(key, value);
            keyMap.put(key, newNode);
            freqMap.computeIfAbsent(1, k -> new DoublyLinkedList())
                    .add(newNode);
            minFreq = 1;
        }
    }

    private void update(Node node) {

        int freq = node.freq;

        DoublyLinkedList list = freqMap.get(freq);
        list.remove(node);

        if (freq == minFreq && list.size == 0) {
            minFreq++;
        }

        node.freq++;

        freqMap.computeIfAbsent(node.freq,
                k -> new DoublyLinkedList()).add(node);
    }
}

⏱ Complexity
Operation	Time
get()	O(1)
put()	O(1)

Space: O(capacity)

